 ("p", "Our number system is a **place-value** system: the value of a digit depends on where it stands, and every place is **10 times** the place on its right. So the digit 7 in 7,000 stands for 7 thousands while in 70 it stands for 7 tens. Writing numbers in groups (periods) makes them easy to read."),
